# SentinelX — Trivy CVE allowlist
#
# Severity gate: CRITICAL, HIGH (enforced in
# .github/workflows/release.yml and .github/workflows/verify-release.yml).
#
# Add ONE entry per line in the form:
#
#     CVE-YYYY-NNNNN
#
# Each entry MUST be preceded by a comment block documenting:
#   1. Affected component / package + version.
#   2. Why it does not affect SentinelX (attack surface, mitigation, etc.).
#   3. Date added + reviewer (GitHub handle).
#   4. Re-review date (max 90 days out — see docs/security/supply-chain.md).
#
# Stale entries (past re-review date) MUST be removed or re-justified.
# Reviewed quarterly by @sentinelx/security.
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EXAMPLE (placeholder — DO NOT KEEP, replace with real triage entries):
#
# Component:    placeholder/example-lib 0.0.0
# Justification: This is a sentinel entry so the file is non-empty and trivy
#                loads the allowlist. It references a reserved CVE ID that
#                will never match a real finding. Replace with real triage.
# Added:         2026-05-30 by @sentinelx-bot
# Re-review by:  2026-08-28
CVE-0000-00000

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AVD-AWS-0104 — Security group rule allows unrestricted egress.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Affected:      deploy/terraform/dev/eks.tf lines 43-65 (EKS cluster SG)
# Justification: EKS control plane MUST reach public AWS APIs (IAM, KMS,
#                CloudWatch, ECR, STS) which live on the public internet.
#                We restrict to 443/tcp (HTTPS) and 53/udp+tcp (DNS)
#                only — all other ports/protocols are denied. Restricting
#                to specific AWS-owned CIDR blocks is operationally
#                fragile (AWS publishes ip-ranges.json but rotation lag
#                causes false negatives).
#                RDS and Redis SGs (rds.tf, elasticache.tf) are already
#                restricted to `aws_vpc.main.cidr_block`.
# Added:         2026-08-04 by @security-review (via nex-erp audit)
# Re-review by:  2026-11-04 — track VPC-endpoint expansion for IAM/STS
AVD-AWS-0104
